      "writtenOn": "2022-07-14T12:45:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought we already had filesystem encryption enabled, why is ecryptfs being used instead?  Are you sure that is supported in Android systems and allowed?",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ed3bb85_e3deed4c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T19:58:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "eCryptfs is not supported by Android. eCryptfs has many known problems and has been mostly abandoned upstream.\n\nAndroid already supports SD card encryption through adoptable storage (https://source.android.com/devices/storage/adoptable), so please use that instead.\n\nPlease also refer to https://source.android.com/devices/architecture/android-kernel-file-system-support.",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2d2d64d_7d06f739",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956079
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T01:59:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to use ecryptfs to implement the SD card encryption function, but ecryptfs cannot be enabled directly in Android systems by set CONFIG_ECRYPT_FS\u003dy，so we want to use ecryptfs by making ecryptfs to ecryptfs.ko. In oeder to make ecryptfs.ko, we must update symbol list.",
      "parentUuid": "70433265_4ced7418",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2b1145e_151a89ca",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956079
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T01:59:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How should I change it? Is there a submission example?",
      "parentUuid": "6c3822d1_c1ad30fe",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "624f44e8_91f2e2ee",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956079
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T01:59:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your answer. We know that, but our sd encryption includes some special features, that mean we must use ecryptfs to support it. And we know Android systems do not directly support ecryptfs, so we want to use it by ecryptfs.ko. That mean we should update some symbol to symbol list. Does this behavior affect the stability of the Android system?",
      "parentUuid": "7ed3bb85_e3deed4c",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22153cb6_5560ca13",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T17:28:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "eCryptfs has many known problems and has been mostly abandoned upstream, and it greatly adds to the KMI that has to be maintained in GKI, so yes it may affect the stability of the system.  It also might not actually solve the problem that you intend it to solve; storage encryption has some very subtle considerations and it is *extremely* easy to come up with something that seems secure but is actually insecure.  We want to make sure that you don\u0027t ship something insecure.  Can you elaborate on what \"special features\" you are trying to accomplish?  Please file a feature bug that describes what you are trying to accomplish and describes in detail the solution you are proposing.",
      "parentUuid": "624f44e8_91f2e2ee",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62182d31_34a2c3b5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-18T20:30:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please also note that eCryptfs doesn\u0027t meet some of the CDD requirements on encryption methods: https://source.android.com/compatibility/12/android-12-cdd#993_encryption_methods.  So as-is, I don\u0027t think that devices using eCryptfs would be able to be certified as Android-compatible.",
      "parentUuid": "22153cb6_5560ca13",
      "revId": "05cd62a21d64ce77addfc2132e9578c36ee43e5f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
